["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>The last thing an old hunter passes down is how to behave when nobody is watching.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Fair chase drawn as a roof on three pillars, from the Boone and Crockett Club definition: ethical, sportsmanlike, lawful. The pursuit of a wild, free ranging animal that keeps a fair chance to escape.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"40,90 200,26 360,90\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"78\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FAIR CHASE</text>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <rect x=\"60\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/><rect x=\"165\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"95\" y=\"170\">Ethical</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"162\">Sporting</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"180\">manner</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"170\">Lawful</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"230\" width=\"320\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wild, free ranging, a fair chance to escape</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Lesson 10 of 10: ethics, respect, and passing it on.</li><li>Fair chase, landowners, waste, poachers, new hunters, and who pays for wildlife.</li><li>Labels and certainty: see <a href=\"#/s/fw-grandpa-01\">lesson 1</a>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: what is in this lesson</summary><ol><li>Fair chase.</li><li>The shot you pass on.</li><li>Leave the gate as you found it.</li><li>Ask first, get it in writing.</li><li>Pack it in, pack it out, leave it better.</li><li>Waste nothing.</li><li>Notch first, knife second.</li><li>Report it, do not confront it.</li><li>Take a new hunter out.</li><li>Your licence buys habitat.</li><li>Then a myth check.</li></ol></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Fair chase drawn as a roof on three pillars, from the Boone and Crockett Club definition: ethical, sportsmanlike, lawful. The pursuit of a wild, free ranging animal that keeps a fair chance to escape.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"40,90 200,26 360,90\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"78\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">FAIR CHASE</text>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <rect x=\"60\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/><rect x=\"165\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"100\" width=\"70\" height=\"130\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"95\" y=\"170\">Ethical</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"162\">Sporting</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"180\">manner</text><text x=\"305\" y=\"170\">Lawful</text>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"230\" width=\"320\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wild, free ranging, a fair chance to escape</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Give the animal a fair chance to get away.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> hunt wild, free animals in an ethical, sporting and lawful way.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. The Boone and Crockett Club's fair chase definition <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>Boone and Crockett Club: fair chase is the \"ethical, sportsmanlike, and lawful pursuit and taking\" of free ranging wild game; an unfair advantage is when the game has no reasonable chance to escape; success is measured by the quality of the chase, not the quantity of game (85%, search preview).</li><li>App: <a href=\"#/s/ethics-fair-chase\">Ethics and fair chase</a>.</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> fair chase is an ethic, not the law. The law is the <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book</a>.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> the Boone and Crockett Club.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Shoot or not flowchart. Four questions in a row: Is it the right species? Is it legal, sex and points? Is there a safe backstop and nothing beyond? Is it in my range, standing right? Four yes answers lead to: take the shot. Any no or any doubt leads to: no shot.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\">\n    <rect x=\"14\" y=\"14\" width=\"250\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"40\">1. Right species?</text>\n    <rect x=\"14\" y=\"66\" width=\"250\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"92\">2. Legal: sex, points?</text>\n    <rect x=\"14\" y=\"118\" width=\"250\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"144\">3. Safe backstop, clear beyond?</text>\n    <rect x=\"14\" y=\"170\" width=\"250\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"196\">4. In my range, good angle?</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M139 54 L139 66\"/><path d=\"M139 106 L139 118\"/><path d=\"M139 158 L139 170\"/><path d=\"M139 210 L139 232\"/>\n    <path d=\"M264 34 L300 34 M264 86 L300 86 M264 138 L300 138 M264 190 L300 190 M300 34 L300 190\"/>\n    <path d=\"M300 112 L318 112\"/>\n  </g>\n  <rect x=\"318\" y=\"88\" width=\"72\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"354\" y=\"109\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No or</text>\n  <text x=\"354\" y=\"126\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">unsure</text>\n  <text x=\"354\" y=\"160\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">NO SHOT</text>\n  <rect x=\"64\" y=\"232\" width=\"150\" height=\"48\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <text x=\"139\" y=\"253\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">All 4 yes</text>\n  <text x=\"139\" y=\"271\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Shot is OK</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"The shot you pass on is the one you never have to explain.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> a bad angle, too far, unsure: let it walk. Pride is not worth a wounded animal.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition (app). Hunter education: be certain of your target <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>This is the app's Grandpa's rule in <a href=\"#/s/ethics-fair-chase\">Ethics and fair chase</a>; \"The shot you pass is never the one you regret\" (<a href=\"#/s/mc-skills-07\">Skills masterclass 7</a>).</li><li>Hunter education's four rules include being certain of the target (85%, <a href=\"#/s/fw-grandpa-01\">lesson 1</a>).</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> never.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> hunters' tradition.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two farm gates. Left: you found it closed, you leave it closed. Right: you found it open, you leave it open, because cattle may need to reach water. Leave every gate the way you found it unless the owner says otherwise.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"170\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"6\">\n    <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"180\"/>\n    <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"180\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M30 110 L170 110 M30 135 L170 135 M30 160 L170 160 M30 160 L170 110\"/>\n    <path d=\"M230 110 L262 70 M230 135 L262 95 M230 160 L262 120 M262 70 L262 120\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"100\" y=\"56\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Found closed</text>\n    <text x=\"100\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#23261f\">Leave it closed</text>\n    <text x=\"300\" y=\"56\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Found open</text>\n    <text x=\"300\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#23261f\">Leave it open</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unless the owner tells you otherwise</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Leave every gate the way you found it.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> closed stays closed, open stays open, unless the owner says otherwise.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. Idaho Fish and Game lists it for hunters on private land <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>Idaho Fish and Game: leave gates the way they are found, park where the landowner wants, stay away from livestock and buildings, know the boundaries (80%, search preview).</li><li>GoHunt's ethics list: leave gates and fences as you found them unless the landowner says otherwise <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>App: \"Every fence has an owner and every gate has a reason\" (<a href=\"#/s/maps-land-status\">Land status maps</a>).</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> if the owner asks you to do something else.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> ranch country everywhere.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Ask the owner</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Which days?</td><td>Last year's yes may not stand</td></tr><tr><td>Which species?</td><td>Deer may be fine, birds not</td></tr><tr><td>Who may come?</td><td>Your brother needs a yes too</td></tr><tr><td>Where to park?</td><td>Gates, crops, livestock</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Never assume last year's permission still stands.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> ask each season, get it in writing, and confirm the details.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. Idaho Fish and Game advises written permission <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>Idaho Fish and Game: get written permission, preferably before the season; confirm days, species and who may come; never assume last year's permission still applies; leave a note with your name, phone and vehicle (80%, search preview).</li><li>Thank the owner whether the answer is yes or no <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>BC rules on private land and posted land: <a href=\"#/s/rb-where-you-can-hunt\">Rule Book: where you can hunt</a>.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> landowner relations programs.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Bring home</th><th>Leave behind</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Wrappers, cans, brass</td><td>Nothing you brought</td></tr><tr><td>Flagging tape you hung (Tip)</td><td>Gates as you found them</td></tr><tr><td>Trash you find (Tip)</td><td>A cleaner spot</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Leave it a little better than you found it.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> carry out everything you carried in, plus a bit of someone else's trash.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. Leave No Trace Canada principle 3 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>Leave No Trace Canada, principle 3, dispose of waste properly: bring back what you carried in; burning trash in a campfire is not acceptable; check campsites for micro waste (85%, search preview).</li><li>Idaho Fish and Game: pick up shell casings; leaving them counts as littering under Idaho law <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. BC littering rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">Rule Book: unlawful acts</a>.</li><li>\"Leave this world a little better than you found it\" is from Robert Baden Powell's last message to Scouts, found after his death in 1941 (80%, Scouting sources, search preview).</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> never.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> Scouting and Leave No Trace.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 322\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Level 2, Apprentice, on the five step ladder Rookie, Apprentice, Hunter, Guide, Old Timer. Goal: first animals, clean shots, all the meat home. Key skills: licence notched on the spot; edible portions packed out and kept cool; passed on at least one shot that was too far or risky. Opinion, not a BC rank.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"322\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Level 2: Apprentice</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"66\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"91\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Old Timer</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"112\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Guide</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"158\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"183\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunter</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"204\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b9a6b\" stroke=\"#6b9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"229\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Apprentice</text>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"250\" width=\"110\" height=\"38\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"69\" y=\"275\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rookie</text>\n<path d=\"M6 290 V30 M132 290 V30\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n<rect x=\"146\" y=\"44\" width=\"244\" height=\"66\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#6b9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"268\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Goal: first animals,</text><text x=\"268\" y=\"93\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">meat home</text>\n<rect x=\"146\" y=\"126\" width=\"244\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#6b9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(172 151) scale(0.8)\"><path d=\"M-14 -18 H8 L16 -10 V18 H-14 Z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-8 -6 H10 M-8 2 H10 M-8 10 H4\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M16 -4 l-6 4 l6 4z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"196\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tag notched on the spot</text>\n<rect x=\"146\" y=\"184\" width=\"244\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#6b9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(172 209) scale(0.8)\"><path d=\"M-18 -4 Q-14 -18 6 -14 Q22 -10 18 6 Q12 18 -6 14 Q-20 10 -18 -4 Z\" fill=\"#c0504d\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M-8 -2 Q2 -8 10 0\" stroke=\"#f5e0d8\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"6\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#f5f0e0\"/></g>\n<text x=\"196\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Edible portions home,</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"223\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">cool</text>\n<rect x=\"146\" y=\"242\" width=\"244\" height=\"50\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#6b9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(172 267) scale(0.8)\"><circle r=\"18\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><path d=\"M-7 -7 l14 14 M7 -7 l-14 14\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></g>\n<text x=\"196\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Passed on a bad shot</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"312\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Opinion: Hunt Mentor&#x27;s ladder, not a BC rank.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"If you shoot it, you eat it.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> take all the edible meat home and use it. Share it if you cannot use it all.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. Hunter education calls it a legal and ethical duty <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>South Dakota hunter education: hunters are \"legally and ethically obligated to harvest as much of the animal as reasonably possible\" (85%, search preview).</li><li>Idaho instructor code: never take more game than you can use <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Montana suggests donating meat you cannot use <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>BC rules on wasting edible game: <a href=\"#/s/rb-unlawful-acts\">Rule Book: unlawful acts</a>.</li><li>App: <a href=\"#/s/meat-care\">Meat care</a>, <a href=\"#/s/cooking\">Cooking wild game</a>.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> hunters' tradition, written into law in many places.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of the order after the kill. Step 1 lights up: notch the species licence, and orange notches appear on the card. Step 2: confirm the animal is dead with the eye touch. Step 3: only then the knife. Final message: licence first, before you touch it.\">\n<rect width=\"400\" height=\"290\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The order never changes</text>\n<g opacity=\"0.25\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0.25;1\" begin=\"0.5s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"164\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f3ead8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"30.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><rect x=\"28\" y=\"100\" width=\"84\" height=\"56\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"28\" y=\"100\" width=\"84\" height=\"13\" fill=\"#e3eedc\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"70\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Deer</text><path d=\"M44 144 h52\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 2\"/><g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"1.2s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M56 100 L62 109 L68 100z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><path d=\"M112 122 L103 128 L112 134z\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/></g><text x=\"70\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Notch</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0.25\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0.25;1\" begin=\"2.8s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"164\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f3ead8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"160.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"160\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><g transform=\"translate(194 134) scale(1.5)\"><path d=\"M-16 0 C-8 -10 8 -10 16 0 C8 10 -8 10 -16 0z\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2.2\"/><circle r=\"5.5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-1.8\" cy=\"-1.8\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#fff\"/></g><path d=\"M244 92 L208 130\" stroke=\"#7a5230\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Confirm dead</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0.25\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0.25;1\" begin=\"5.0s\" dur=\"0.4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"270\" y=\"50\" width=\"120\" height=\"164\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f3ead8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"290.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"290\" y=\"75\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><g transform=\"translate(330 128) rotate(-35)\"><path d=\"M-44 -2 C-20 -10 6 -8 14 -6 L14 6 C-8 6 -30 6 -44 -2z\" fill=\"#c9ccc6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M-40 -2 C-20 -6 0 -6 12 -4\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><rect x=\"14\" y=\"-7\" width=\"5\" height=\"14\" rx=\"1\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"19\" y=\"-6\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/></g><text x=\"330\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Knife</text></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"2.4s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M140.0 132.0 L129.0 126.0 L129.0 138.1z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"4.6s\" dur=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><path d=\"M270.0 132.0 L259.0 126.0 L259.0 138.1z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/></g>\n<g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"6.2s\" dur=\"0.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><rect x=\"8\" y=\"232\" width=\"384\" height=\"37\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"256.4\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Licence first, before you touch it</text></g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Notch, confirm, then the knife. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Notch first, knife second.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> cancel your licence on the spot, before you touch the knife.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition (app). The tagging rule itself is law (see the Rule Book).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><aside class=\"callout warn\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The official regulations are the law.</p></aside><ul><li>This is the app's Grandpa's rule in <a href=\"#/s/after-the-shot\">After the shot</a> and <a href=\"#/s/mc-white-tailed-deer-10\">White tailed deer masterclass 10</a>.</li><li>The exact tagging and reporting rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-after-the-kill\">Rule Book: after the kill</a>.</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> never.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> BC hunters' habit, built on the licence rules.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Do</th><th>Do not</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Note date, time, place</td><td>Confront the person</td></tr><tr><td>Note plates, gear, actions</td><td>Follow them</td></tr><tr><td>Call RAPP (Report All Poachers and Polluters)</td><td>Post it online first</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (opinion)</div><p>\"A poacher steals from every hunter. Report him, do not fight him.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> write down the details and call the <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"RAPP\">RAPP</button> line.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> opinion. BC's line: 1 877 952 7277 (95%, Rule Book).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>RAPP (Report All Poachers and Polluters) line: 1 877 952 7277, 24 hours (95%, synopsis page 2, via the app's Rule Book and <a href=\"#/s/rs-predator-sign\">Predator sign</a>).</li><li>BC government: never confront or try to stop a suspect; record date, time, location, actions, gear, vehicle and witnesses (85%, gov.bc.ca page, search preview).</li><li>If someone is in danger, call 911 first <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>\"Post it online first\" in the table is the app's advice, not the government's (Tip).</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> the BC Conservation Officer Service.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>BC Wildlife Federation</th><th>What it is</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Learn to Hunt orientation</td><td>Monthly, in person</td></tr><tr><td>Learn to Hunt Academy</td><td>2 day course</td></tr><tr><td>Volunteer instructors</td><td>5 years hunting, PAL</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Somebody took you. Take somebody.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> pass it on: mentor a new hunter, when you are ready.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. Mentoring is the core of hunter recruitment programs <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>BC Wildlife Federation runs a monthly Learn to Hunt and Fish orientation and a 2 day Learn to Hunt Academy; volunteer instructors need at least 5 years of hunting and a valid PAL (Possession and Acquisition Licence) (80%, search preview).</li><li>Recruitment programs (often called R3: recruit, retain, reactivate) find keeping new hunters is the hard part; peer mentors help (70%, NC State researcher, search preview).</li><li>App: <a href=\"#/s/season-planning\">Season planning</a>. Wait until you have a few seasons yourself (Tip).</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> take a new hunter only where you know the rules and the ground well (Tip).</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> hunting families and clubs.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Flow chart. Your BC hunting licence includes a conservation surcharge. The surcharge goes to the Habitat Conservation Trust Foundation, set up after hunters and anglers asked for it. The foundation funds fish, wildlife and habitat projects across BC.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"30\" width=\"360\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"54\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Your licence</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"74\" fill=\"#23261f\">includes a conservation surcharge</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"120\" width=\"360\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"144\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Habitat Conservation Trust</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"164\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Foundation (HCTF)</text>\n    <rect x=\"20\" y=\"210\" width=\"360\" height=\"54\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"234\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffffff\">Fish, wildlife and habitat</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"254\" fill=\"#ffffff\">projects across BC</text>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"116\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"206\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M192 108 L200 120 L208 108 Z M192 198 L200 210 L208 198 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (tradition)</div><p>\"Hunters paid for the wild.\"</p></aside><ul><li><strong>Means:</strong> part of what you pay for licences goes straight to fish and wildlife habitat.</li><li><strong>Label:</strong> tradition. BC surcharges go to the Habitat Conservation Trust Foundation <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why, when it is wrong, where it comes from</summary><ul><li>Surcharges on BC hunting, angling, trapping and guiding licences are dedicated to the Habitat Conservation Trust Foundation (HCTF); the fund began in 1981 after hunters and anglers asked for it (80%, Union of BC Municipalities and news reports, search preview).</li><li>The HCTF says the surcharge funds over 100 fish, wildlife and habitat projects each year <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Exact surcharge amounts: <a href=\"#/s/rb-licences-fees\">Rule Book: licences and fees</a>.</li><li><strong>When it is wrong:</strong> base licence fees go elsewhere; only the surcharge is dedicated <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Where it comes from:</strong> the North American conservation tradition.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Myth meter. A scale in three parts. Left, orange: myth, science says no. Middle, light: mixed, studies disagree or it depends. Right, green: holds up, evidence supports it. Each saying in the myth check gets a place on this scale.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"40\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Myth meter</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"100\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <rect x=\"140\" y=\"100\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"260\" y=\"100\" width=\"120\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"100\" width=\"360\" height=\"60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"137\" fill=\"#ffffff\">MYTH</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"137\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">MIXED</text>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"137\" fill=\"#ffffff\">HOLDS UP</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"80\" y=\"190\">Science</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"208\">says no</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"190\">Studies</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"208\">disagree</text>\n    <text x=\"320\" y=\"190\">Evidence</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"208\">backs it</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tradition is not proof. Check the source.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Saying</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\"Fair chase is the law\"</td><td>Myth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Last year's permission still counts\"</td><td>Myth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr><tr><td>\"Licence money all goes to government\"</td><td>Myth <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the evidence for each</summary><ul><li><strong>Fair chase:</strong> an ethic defined by the Boone and Crockett Club; the law is the synopsis and the Wildlife Act <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>. Ethics often ask more than the law.</li><li><strong>Permission:</strong> Idaho Fish and Game: never assume last year's permission still applies <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><strong>Licence money:</strong> BC conservation surcharges are dedicated to the Habitat Conservation Trust Foundation <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two farm gates. Left: you found it closed, you leave it closed. Right: you found it open, you leave it open, because cattle may need to reach water. Leave every gate the way you found it unless the owner says otherwise.\">\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"170\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"6\">\n    <line x1=\"30\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"180\"/>\n    <line x1=\"230\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"230\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"370\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"370\" y2=\"180\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" fill=\"none\">\n    <path d=\"M30 110 L170 110 M30 135 L170 135 M30 160 L170 160 M30 160 L170 110\"/>\n    <path d=\"M230 110 L262 70 M230 135 L262 95 M230 160 L262 120 M262 70 L262 120\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"16\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"100\" y=\"56\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Found closed</text>\n    <text x=\"100\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#23261f\">Leave it closed</text>\n    <text x=\"300\" y=\"56\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Found open</text>\n    <text x=\"300\" y=\"256\" fill=\"#23261f\">Leave it open</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Unless the owner tells you otherwise</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Found it closed, leave it closed. Found it open, leave it open.\"</li><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Notch first, knife second.\"</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> 1981: the year hunters and anglers got the conservation fund started <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Ethical, sporting, lawful:</strong> the three legs of fair chase <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><strong>RAPP</strong> (Report All Poachers and Polluters): 1 877 952 7277 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li><strong>Somebody took you. Take somebody.</strong></li></ul><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Assuming last year's yes still stands.</li><li>Leaving brass and flagging tape in the bush.</li><li>Confronting a poacher instead of reporting.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Save the RAPP number in your phone today. Write a thank you note to a landowner after your next hunt.</p></aside></details>","<ul><li>Boone and Crockett Club, <a href=\"https://boone-crockett.org/principles-fair-chase\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Principles of fair chase</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Idaho Fish and Game, <a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/press/hunters-ask-first-and-treat-landowners-respect-when-hunting-private-land-you-may-get-invited\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunters ask first and treat landowners with respect</a> and <a href=\"https://idfg.idaho.gov/press/respect-and-courtesy-are-essential-when-hunting-private-land\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Respect and courtesy are essential</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>GoHunt, <a href=\"https://www.gohunt.com/browse/hunting-101/wildlife-management-and-hunter-ethics/the-4-rs-of-ethical-hunters\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The 4 Rs of ethical hunters</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Leave No Trace Canada, <a href=\"https://leavenotrace.ca/principles\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The seven principles</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Wikipedia, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaving_the_world_a_better_place\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Leaving the world a better place</a>, and World Scouting, <a href=\"https://www.scout.org/node/2697\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Baden Powell legacy</a>, search preview (75 to 80%)</li></ul><ul><li>South Dakota hunter education on the Hunter Ed course site, <a href=\"https://www.hunter-ed.com/southdakota/studyGuide/Wanton-Waste-Law/20204303_258113/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Wanton waste law</a>, and Idaho, <a href=\"https://tag.idaho.gov/sites/default/files/instructor-code-ethics.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">instructor code of ethics</a>, search preview (75 to 85%)</li></ul>","<ul><li>BC Conservation Officer Service, <a href=\"https://www2.gov.bc.ca/gov/content/environment/natural-resource-stewardship/natural-resource-law-enforcement/conservation-officer-service/cos-rapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Report All Poachers and Polluters</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>; number via the app Rule Book, synopsis page 2 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li></ul><ul><li>BC Wildlife Federation, <a href=\"https://bcwf.bc.ca/learn-to-hunt-academy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn to Hunt Academy</a> and <a href=\"https://bcwf.bc.ca/learn-to-hunt-and-fish/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Learn to Hunt and Fish</a>, search preview <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li></ul><ul><li>NC State University, R3 research news, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li></ul><ul><li>Union of BC Municipalities, <a href=\"https://www.ubcm.ca/convention-resolutions/resolutions/resolutions-database/allocation-wildlife-revenues-conservation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Allocation of wildlife revenues to conservation</a>, and Castanet, <a href=\"https://www.castanetkamloops.net/news/Opinion/385242/Hunters-anglers-pushed-hard-to-create-conservation-institutions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Hunters and anglers pushed hard to create conservation institutions</a>, search preview (75 to 80%)</li></ul><ul><li>Research notes: <code>research/2026-10-11-fw-grandpa.md</code>.</li></ul>"]